4. Priya Nair (author of the formatting commit and of the reverted MergePatchLite) is credited with at most 0.5% (absent is correct), and github-actions[bot] is not ranked as an owner of the code. FAIL if Priya is above 1%, or if the bot appears as a ranked author.
5. The answer says what it left out or merged: it must state that it ignored or looked through the formatting/whitespace commit, that it merged identities (at least the Tomás Ibarra pair), and that bot-authored lines (about 5 lines) are excluded or reported separately. FAIL if any of these three statements is missing, or if the answer presents commit counts as the ownership measure.

