| | 31 other authors | 121 | 3.4% |

**Per file**
- `cJSON.c`: Max Bruckner 2,587 lines. Next are Kevin Branigan (149), Alan Wang (112), tomasi (66) and Dave Gamble (62).
- `cJSON.h`: Max Bruckner 112 lines. Next are Mike Jerris (51), Dave Gamble (49), Alan Wang (19) and Zach Hindes (17).

**Project-level bus factor: 1.** Max Bruckner alone owns more than 50% of the surviving lines. The next four authors together own about 13%.

**Notes on the method**
- **Clang-format commit:** `413c6d1` (Priya Nair) is in `.git-blame-ignore-revs`. I ran blame with and without that file and got identical results. Priya Nair has 0 surviving lines either way, because `-w` already ignores whitespace-only changes. The reformat did not move credit.
- **`-M -C` flags:** These follow moved and copied lines, so code that was only relocated stays with its original author.
- **Original author:** Dave Gamble wrote cJSON originally, but only 3.1% of his lines survive. Max Bruckner rewrote most of the code during his maintainership.
- **What blame can't show:** It credits whoever last changed a line in a meaningful way. It doesn't show who understands the design. Someone who made many small edits to a line may own it in blame without having authored it.
- **Not checked:** I did not check whether Max Bruckner or the other authors are still active. That would need `git log --author` with a date filter. I also did not count dependents, because this is a two-file library with no meaningful import graph.

